   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "WAN 2.2 14B uses two models: a high-noise expert for the first half of sampling (layout, motion) and a low-noise expert for the rest (detail). Bend each MODEL separately; here only the high-noise expert is bent, in its middle blocks (40 blocks: ~17-24), so the layout changes and the details stay clean.\n\nEXPERIMENTAL: the video bending nodes were validated on tiny random-weight WAN models only, not yet on real WAN weights. Please report what you see.\n\nModels: wan2.2_t2v_high_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors and wan2.2_t2v_low_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors from https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.2_ComfyUI_Repackaged (diffusion_models); text encoder and VAE as for WAN 2.1 (wan_2.1_vae)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
